<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bariba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bariba are a people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borgu">Borgu</a>, in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. In the early centuries of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> they exerted military pressure on Oyo from the north-west. Conflict with the Bariba and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe</a> shaped Oyo's early history.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The early centuries were precarious: Oyo faced persistent pressure from the Nupe kingdom to the north-east and the <b>Bariba of Borgu</b> to the north-west, and in the early sixteenth century a crushing defeat by the Nupe forced the ruling dynasty into roughly eighty years of exile, much of…</blockquote><a href="/empire/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The king of Bussa ruled over Busa-speaking and <b>Bariba</b> subjects and controlled crossings and rapids on the Niger.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-bussa">Kingdom of Bussa</a></li><li><blockquote>Nikki was founded by Wasangari horsemen who imposed their rule on <b>Bariba</b> farming communities of eastern Borgu, probably in the 16th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-nikki">Kingdom of Nikki</a></li><li><blockquote>Sabe traded with the Oyo Empire, Borgu and the coast, and was exposed to raids from the Kingdom of Dahomey and the <b>Bariba</b> of Borgu.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-sabe">Kingdom of Sabe</a></li></ul></section>
